REFUTED 2026-09-29 (RO_1/2/3: 982/830/991 strong flash frames, 3 of 3 dirty, vs ~480-600 default) - NOT a surgical
test of "an older copy overwrites a newer overlapping resolve". The same targets are re-resolved every frame, so each new
resolve fully covered the previous pending copy of the SAME target and this change made it skip everything: landings fell
from ~20,000 per 5 s window (410 ms of copy work) to ~123 (1.5 ms). It effectively DROPPED nearly all superseded copies,
which 0.2.11 already found causes the violet flash. Reading (auditor + session 4c): the late copies REPAIR guest memory;
the fault is the ORDER of copy-back relative to its resolve (waiting on resolves >= 1..4096 KB lands fewer copies,
8.5k-14k, and is clean), not the count and not CPU reads. Kept for the record; do not apply.

